  "verdict": "Independent validation (parameters as shipped) FAILS the pre-set 60 mV voltage criterion at all four rates (MAE 67-121 mV) (capacity within 5 % passes at all rates). A one-parameter calibration of the exchange-current scale (x2) brings MAE to 42-55 mV at all rates (paper's own model 20-48 mV) - that is calibration on the same data, not validation. Consequence for S3: capacity-vs-rate trends usable at +/-5 %; absolute voltages carry >= +/-0.1 V uncertainty until kinetics are measured (GITT/EIS) for the real electrodes.",
